WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.781
<i>In 197X...</i>

2
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.389
<i>On an island near the Aleutians...</i>

3
00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:28.820
<i>A second underground nuclear</i>
<i>bomb test was carried out.</i>

4
00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.227
<i>This is what happened...</i>

5
00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:02.193
<i>The effects of the explosion were widespread.</i>
<i>affecting even Monster Island in the South Pacific.</i>

6
00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:04.450
GODZiLLA VS MEGALON
(GOJiRA TAi MEGARO)

7
00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.214
Brother!

8
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.988
Hey. that looks like fun.
Want to try it?

9
00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.851
Sure. why not?!

10
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.255
A drink?
- Sure.

11
00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.046
An earthquake...

12
00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.111
Roku!

13
00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.347
<i>It's an earthquake!</i>
<i>Come to shore!</i>

14
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.594
It won't move!

15
00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.528
Hey. the rocket!

16
00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.407
Brother!

17
00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.751
Brother. it's not working!

18
00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.349
Hey. what's that?!

19
00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.690
Hey. Roku!

20
00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.230
Hey. over there!

21
00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:39.509
<i>And now we bring you the</i>
<i>latest news reports...</i>

22
00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.778
<i>The National Seismic</i>
<i>Institute believes...</i>

23
00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:46.550
<i>... the earthquakes are an effect</i>
<i>from the second nuclear bomb test.</i>

24
00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.126
<i>They also warn that more</i>
<i>tremors are expected.</i>

25
00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.085
It's incredible. isn't it?

26
00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.597
To think that all this was a
result of the nuclear explosion.

27
00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:55.758
That's right.

28
00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:58.437
We'll wind up just like
the Mu Continent...

29
00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:00.801
...and Lamoria if we
don't watch out.

30
00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.999
It'll be the end of all mankind.

31
00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:06.637
What...? What do you mean about
Lamoria and the Mu Continent?

32
00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:10.582
It's like this...
About 3 million years ago...

33
00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:13.981
...Lamoria was in the Indian ocean.
and Mu was in the Pacific.

34
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.951
Both were great civilizations. until
a big earthquake destroyed them.

35
00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:23.490
However. most of this is legend. and
no one is certain if they ever existed.

36
00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:47.985
Hey. wouldn't it be interesting if the
earthquake destroyed your robot?

37
00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:50.719
You're really funny...
Hey...

38
00:10:00.967 --> 00:10:01.956
Brother!

39
00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:02.760
What is it?

40
00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:04.927
The door was open.
That's strange...

41
00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:20.980
Damn!

42
00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:31.927
Damn!

43
00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:51.947
Professor! Professor!

44
00:10:53.953 --> 00:10:54.851
Are you okay?

45
00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:56.147
I'm alright.

46
00:10:58.457 --> 00:10:59.287
Roku!

47
00:11:01.227 --> 00:11:02.660
He seems to be okay as well.

48
00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:04.394
Right!

49
00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:24.081
Damn!

50
00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:56.041
<i>Damn. they really made a</i>
<i>mess of this place.</i>

51
00:12:18.838 --> 00:12:22.205
Brother. those guys made
a mess of my room.

52
00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:22.898
How about here?

53
00:12:24.009 --> 00:12:26.239
Every room seems to be messed up.
but nothing was stolen.

54
00:12:26.378 --> 00:12:27.208
Really?

55
00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.110
However. we should make
a thorough check.

56
00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:54.899
Brother!

57
00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:57.871
There's some funny powder
on the floor here.

58
00:13:02.047 --> 00:13:03.412
What do you think it is?

59
00:13:05.818 --> 00:13:07.046
It looks like sand.

60
00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:10.879
Damn!

61
00:14:15.888 --> 00:14:17.480
This situation is awfully strange.

62
00:14:19.024 --> 00:14:21.185
They wouldn't go to
this trouble for nothing...

63
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.658
...so they must have been
after something of yours.

64
00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.389
What's that?

65
00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:29.058
It's a button I got from
one of those guys.

66
00:14:33.706 --> 00:14:36.800
Brother. this looks like the same color
as that sand I found on the floor.

67
00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.768
You're right.

68
00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:41.311
You found some sand?

69
00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:47.210
What is this?

70
00:14:50.856 --> 00:14:52.153
It's red sand.

71
00:14:52.658 --> 00:14:56.025
It must have been from their shoes.
We found it next to the robot.

72
00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:43.970
Good afternoon!
- Hey!

73
00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.012
What are you making?

74
00:15:49.348 --> 00:15:50.781
A Baby-Rider.

75
00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.478
Baby-Rider?

76
00:15:52.718 --> 00:15:54.481
You're the one who races.
Can't you tell?

77
00:15:54.653 --> 00:15:56.678
Nah. I'm just an amateur.

78
00:15:57.323 --> 00:16:00.759
I'm through with the water.
I'm sticking to land. where it's safe.

79
00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.750
Do you think it will work?

80
00:16:03.195 --> 00:16:04.662
You can bet on it!

81
00:16:06.098 --> 00:16:06.860
You think it's okay?

82
00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:08.499
It's alright.
I'm going out!

83
00:16:15.874 --> 00:16:17.899
I'm going to give
it a test run. Bye-bye!

84
00:16:18.577 --> 00:16:19.566
Be careful!

85
00:16:31.724 --> 00:16:32.850
<i>Come in...</i>

86
00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:39.929
Good afternoon...
oh. it looks like it's finished!

87
00:16:40.432 --> 00:16:42.024
It will be completed soon.

88
00:16:42.601 --> 00:16:44.831
We've finally finished
examining the sand.

89
00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:45.902
What did you find?

90
00:16:46.271 --> 00:16:48.569
It comes from a stratus
30 kilometers beneath the sea.

91
00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:50.373
Huh? Is that true?!

92
00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:53.478
Yes. The only other place that
has that sand is on Easter Island.

93
00:16:53.712 --> 00:16:55.839
Easter Island? Where is that?

94
00:16:57.483 --> 00:17:00.577
<i>It's a small uninhabited island about</i>
<i>1300 kilometers southeast of Tahiti.</i>

95
00:17:02.087 --> 00:17:05.545
However. it's mostly famous for
a discovery that was made there.

96
00:17:05.924 --> 00:17:08.119
<i>They had found rows of 20 meter</i>
<i>high statues overlooking the sea.</i>

97
00:17:09.428 --> 00:17:11.862
They're said to be over
three million years old.

98
00:17:15.667 --> 00:17:18.329
That doesn't help us get any closer
to the people behind all this.

99
00:17:28.213 --> 00:17:30.681
<i>It's working!</i>
<i>Hey. it's working!</i>

100
00:17:37.322 --> 00:17:39.017
Congratulations!
You've done it at last!

101
00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:40.724
How's this?

102
00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.490
I think I'll name the
robot. Jet Jaguar.

103
00:17:43.962 --> 00:17:46.089
<i>Jet Jaguar...?</i>
<i>That's not a bad name.</i>

104
00:17:46.498 --> 00:17:47.795
<i>Hey. let's go!</i>
<i>Let's try it out!</i>

105
00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.397
<i>Let's go try it out!</i>

106
00:18:10.622 --> 00:18:11.589
Help me!

107
00:18:19.064 --> 00:18:20.998
There are TV cameras
in its eyes.

108
00:18:21.266 --> 00:18:24.258
It's also equipped with
evasion devices...

109
00:18:24.436 --> 00:18:25.926
...so it will always get
out of your way.

110
00:18:26.105 --> 00:18:28.096
That's great!

111
00:18:29.341 --> 00:18:32.606
As far as I'm concerned.
it can have the right of way!

112
00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:45.552
<i>Come in. the door's open.</i>

113
00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:02.036
It's them!
- Damn!

114
00:19:19.291 --> 00:19:21.020
Seatopia. Seatopia.

115
00:19:21.693 --> 00:19:23.888
<i>This is Seatopia.</i>
<i>We are receiving you.</i>

116
00:19:24.563 --> 00:19:25.996
Everything has gone well.

117
00:19:27.132 --> 00:19:30.659
We have managed to occupy the laboratory
and captured the inventor as well.

118
00:19:31.236 --> 00:19:33.227
Good work.
You've done well.

119
00:19:34.039 --> 00:19:37.099
Program the robot so it can
guide Megalon to the target.

120
00:20:45.844 --> 00:20:46.970
My people...

121
00:20:48.013 --> 00:20:51.847
Today. Seatopia goes to war.

122
00:20:52.851 --> 00:20:56.218
After three million years of peace.
we finally have to fight.

123
00:20:56.955 --> 00:21:02.416
We do not want to make war. but the
people of earth leave us no choice.

124
00:21:03.729 --> 00:21:06.459
With their nuclear tests. they've already
destroyed a third of our country.

125
00:21:07.633 --> 00:21:10.431
We must fight for the
sake of Seatopia!

126
00:21:10.969 --> 00:21:14.996
We will give the earth people
a taste of their own medicine.

127
00:21:15.807 --> 00:21:21.439
But now. Seatopia goes to
war for the sake of peace!

128
00:21:22.114 --> 00:21:24.014
For the sake of Seatopia!

129
00:21:28.787 --> 00:21:29.719
Megalon!

130
00:21:31.023 --> 00:21:31.853
Megalon!

131
00:21:34.059 --> 00:21:35.856
Wake up. Megalon!

132
00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:42.999
Rise to the surface of the earth!

133
00:21:43.502 --> 00:21:49.930
Destroy all of man! In the name of
peace. the honor and sake of Seatopia!

134
00:21:57.616 --> 00:21:59.413
Go. Megalon!

135
00:23:59.271 --> 00:24:00.238
Brother!

136
00:24:02.507 --> 00:24:03.838
Where is Jinko?

137
00:24:04.976 --> 00:24:06.170
He's not here.

138
00:24:14.052 --> 00:24:14.984
It's metal.

139
00:24:15.754 --> 00:24:17.847
They've got us in a
metal container.

140
00:24:18.657 --> 00:24:21.922
What do we do. brother?
I think they're going to kill us both!

141
00:24:22.093 --> 00:24:23.390
I don't think so. Roku.

142
00:24:24.996 --> 00:24:28.056
In the meantime. try to help
me with these ropes.

143
00:25:17.048 --> 00:25:17.810
Not yet!

144
00:25:17.983 --> 00:25:18.881
<i>A little more!</i>

145
00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:38.400
Brother!

146
00:25:38.803 --> 00:25:40.430
Roku. are you okay?

147
00:25:42.941 --> 00:25:43.873
Hang in there!

148
00:25:49.314 --> 00:25:51.578
How much longer until
we get to the lake?

149
00:25:51.783 --> 00:25:55.150
Well. it should be
around an hour. right?

150
00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.083
Yes.

151
00:25:56.421 --> 00:25:58.048
This is really unusual...

152
00:25:58.256 --> 00:26:02.215
why would you want this container
taken to the crack in the lakebed?

153
00:26:02.827 --> 00:26:04.317
What's in the thing anyway?

154
00:26:08.533 --> 00:26:12.060
I guess we're not supposed
to know what's inside that thing.

155
00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:14.467
We should just keep quiet
and take our �100.000.

156
00:26:28.687 --> 00:26:29.676
Damn!

157
00:26:39.531 --> 00:26:41.089
Where did you take the others?

158
00:26:44.569 --> 00:26:45.536
Brother. I did it!

159
00:26:46.638 --> 00:26:47.900
Thank you. Roku.

160
00:27:00.619 --> 00:27:02.484
The robot has made it
to the lakebed.

161
00:27:03.788 --> 00:27:04.755
Everything is ready.

162
00:27:04.956 --> 00:27:05.786
<i>Roger.</i>

163
00:27:06.591 --> 00:27:10.186
The inventor will be there soon.
He's on his way now with his brother.

164
00:27:10.362 --> 00:27:14.799
<i>Roger. The elevator's on its way up and should</i>
<i>emerge from the crack in the lakebed soon.</i>

165
00:27:17.702 --> 00:27:19.294
Where are you taking
my two friends?

166
00:27:19.537 --> 00:27:20.799
To the land of Seatopia.

167
00:27:21.973 --> 00:27:23.099
Seatopia?

168
00:27:23.274 --> 00:27:24.172
That's right.

169
00:27:24.943 --> 00:27:27.537
It's a country below the
surface of the sea.

170
00:27:27.846 --> 00:27:32.715
It was engulfed by an earthquake 3.000.000
years ago. Most of our people survived.

171
00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:39.154
We've created our own oxygen supply.
and later we constructed our own sun.

172
00:27:39.324 --> 00:27:40.814
Then the legends are true!

173
00:27:41.026 --> 00:27:44.587
We are a very advanced people.
Our scientists are far more superior to yours.

174
00:27:44.796 --> 00:27:47.458
If you're so superior.
why steal a robot?

175
00:27:47.832 --> 00:27:49.459
Seatopia doesn't have many people.

176
00:27:50.001 --> 00:27:53.129
For the sake of our peace...

177
00:27:53.271 --> 00:27:55.205
...we needed to steal it
to create an army.

178
00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:57.773
Really? Then why did you
kidnap my friends?

179
00:28:29.374 --> 00:28:31.069
Now you're going to tell me
where my friends are!

180
00:28:31.776 --> 00:28:33.539
Speak! Speak!

181
00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:35.639
Where are they?!

182
00:28:37.615 --> 00:28:38.946
Haven't had enough?!

183
00:28:40.351 --> 00:28:41.545
Container...

184
00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:43.180
Truck...

185
00:29:05.210 --> 00:29:06.643
Alright. you're free now.

186
00:29:10.315 --> 00:29:11.247
<i>Brother!</i>

187
00:29:29.934 --> 00:29:30.457
Ouch!

188
00:29:31.402 --> 00:29:31.959
Are you okay?

189
00:29:49.287 --> 00:29:51.050
Unit one! Unit one!

190
00:29:51.723 --> 00:29:53.816
<i>This is unit one.</i>
<i>This is unit one.</i>

191
00:29:54.993 --> 00:29:56.756
I'm calling from the
robot laboratory.

192
00:29:57.162 --> 00:29:59.392
The young prisoner I
was holding has escaped.

193
00:29:59.998 --> 00:30:02.660
He will try to rescue the
professor and the robot.

194
00:30:02.901 --> 00:30:04.061
You must stop him!

195
00:33:26.904 --> 00:33:28.838
Megalon has arrived
on the surface.

196
00:33:29.807 --> 00:33:31.900
I am going to instruct
it to attack Tokyo.

197
00:33:32.076 --> 00:33:32.940
<i>Roger.</i>

198
00:34:12.250 --> 00:34:14.081
<i>This is a special news flash.</i>

199
00:34:14.619 --> 00:34:16.644
<i>Today at 1:30 PM...</i>

200
00:34:16.821 --> 00:34:19.847
<i>... a new monster has emerged</i>
<i>from the lakebed of Lake Kiriyama.</i>

201
00:34:20.024 --> 00:34:24.461
<i>At its last sighting it was heading east.</i>
<i>It has already attacked numerous villages.</i>

202
00:34:24.629 --> 00:34:26.290
They can't be serious!

203
00:34:26.464 --> 00:34:28.864
Hey. why don't we take the container
to the dam and dump it. okay?

204
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:32.026
That would be just as good
as taking it to the lake.

205
00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:33.829
No. keep driving.

206
00:34:34.005 --> 00:34:34.972
That's suicide!

207
00:36:14.705 --> 00:36:15.694
Unit!

208
00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:17.172
Halt!

209
00:36:31.222 --> 00:36:32.689
<i>Take positions!</i>

210
00:37:08.626 --> 00:37:10.685
Brother. it feels like
we've stopped.

211
00:37:17.368 --> 00:37:18.300
Brother!

212
00:37:42.627 --> 00:37:43.787
What was that noise?

213
00:37:59.677 --> 00:38:00.701
The monster!

214
00:38:11.989 --> 00:38:13.854
You've got to get us out of here!

215
00:38:13.958 --> 00:38:15.220
Hurry. there's a monster coming!

216
00:38:15.393 --> 00:38:16.451
What happened to the foreign guy?

217
00:38:16.627 --> 00:38:17.491
We threw him out of the truck!

218
00:38:36.447 --> 00:38:37.937
We need to lower the container!

219
00:38:38.115 --> 00:38:39.707
That's crazy!

220
00:38:40.251 --> 00:38:41.240
Please. use the controls!

221
00:38:41.419 --> 00:38:42.477
No way!

222
00:39:59.463 --> 00:40:00.225
Damn!

223
00:41:02.092 --> 00:41:04.287
Roku! Roku!

224
00:41:05.362 --> 00:41:06.590
Are you okay?

225
00:41:08.732 --> 00:41:10.495
Professor! Professor!

226
00:41:12.937 --> 00:41:13.528
Are you alright?

227
00:41:13.704 --> 00:41:15.001
It's you. Jinko?

228
00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:36.125
Didn't that look just
like Jet Jaguar?

229
00:41:36.594 --> 00:41:38.721
You're right.
That's Jet Jaguar!

230
00:41:39.530 --> 00:41:41.657
Damn. they must have
reprogrammed him!

231
00:41:42.099 --> 00:41:45.626
If we could get Jet Jaguar to
contact Godzilla. he would stop him!

232
00:41:46.136 --> 00:41:48.195
Alright. that's what we'll do.

233
00:41:48.372 --> 00:41:49.168
What?!

234
00:41:51.075 --> 00:41:53.669
This is an ultra-sonic computer
transmitter that I made...

235
00:41:53.878 --> 00:41:55.971
...in case the main
computer failed.

236
00:41:58.349 --> 00:41:59.611
It's too late!

237
00:41:59.850 --> 00:42:00.680
What's the matter?

238
00:42:00.885 --> 00:42:03.376
The ultra-sonic frequency can only
reach Jet Jaguar in the line of sight.

239
00:42:03.988 --> 00:42:05.046
Open fire!

240
00:43:34.712 --> 00:43:37.681
You want Jet Jaguar
to find Godzilla?

241
00:43:37.915 --> 00:43:38.677
Yes.

242
00:43:39.583 --> 00:43:43.986
But. isn't Jet Jaguar's computer
system controlled by the enemy?

243
00:43:44.254 --> 00:43:45.687
It is. but my
ultra-sonic transmitter...

244
00:43:45.856 --> 00:43:48.086
...should override the main
computer's commands.

245
00:43:48.225 --> 00:43:48.919
I'm sure of it!

246
00:43:49.093 --> 00:43:50.025
Okay. we'll try it.

247
00:43:50.160 --> 00:43:50.717
Yes. sir!

248
00:45:18.015 --> 00:45:19.277
Jet Jaguar. stop!

249
00:45:26.857 --> 00:45:28.916
I've lost control of the robot!

250
00:45:29.460 --> 00:45:32.486
Go to Monster Island.
Find Godzilla and bring him here.

251
00:45:39.303 --> 00:45:41.100
This is an emergency...

252
00:45:41.238 --> 00:45:44.469
The robot's control has been
restored to the professor.

253
00:45:44.708 --> 00:45:46.369
What is the robot doing now?

254
00:45:46.510 --> 00:45:48.569
<i>It's heading to Monster</i>
<i>Island to find Godzilla.</i>

255
00:45:48.946 --> 00:45:49.878
I see...

256
00:45:50.314 --> 00:45:52.282
Stay in the robot's laboratory.

257
00:45:53.250 --> 00:45:56.549
You may still have a chance
to regain control of the robot.

258
00:45:56.687 --> 00:45:57.551
<i>Roger.</i>

259
00:45:58.355 --> 00:46:02.849
I want you to contact Star-Hunter Galaxy M-1.
Have them send us Gigan right away.

260
00:46:03.360 --> 00:46:03.826
Yes. sir.

261
00:46:03.994 --> 00:46:07.020
Also. I want you to contact
our base at Easter Island.

262
00:46:25.182 --> 00:46:26.979
The monster appears to be
running all over the place.

263
00:46:27.117 --> 00:46:29.585
Yes. that's because it's
lost its controller.

264
00:47:53.070 --> 00:47:54.469
Brother. over there!

265
00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:05.914
Excuse me.
Good afternoon.

266
00:48:09.987 --> 00:48:11.648
Excuse me.

267
00:48:13.523 --> 00:48:15.388
There's nobody in the store.

268
00:48:15.525 --> 00:48:16.549
That's strange.

269
00:48:23.600 --> 00:48:25.727
We can't help it.
We'll bring this back soon.

270
00:51:34.491 --> 00:51:35.219
Let's go.

271
00:52:33.850 --> 00:52:34.782
Damn!

272
00:52:59.442 --> 00:53:00.374
Roku!

273
00:53:17.994 --> 00:53:19.086
Brother!

274
00:53:19.696 --> 00:53:20.788
Oh. you did it!

275
00:53:22.199 --> 00:53:23.359
Everything is working out well.

276
00:53:23.533 --> 00:53:24.932
Jet Jaguar has found Godzilla.

277
00:53:25.068 --> 00:53:25.830
Really?

278
00:53:28.972 --> 00:53:31.372
The monster is getting closer.
We have to hurry out of here.

279
00:53:31.541 --> 00:53:32.667
What about this guy?

280
00:53:32.842 --> 00:53:34.275
Let's take him.
Come on!

281
00:53:39.316 --> 00:53:40.749
Hold him tight!

282
00:53:44.254 --> 00:53:46.188
Forget about him.
We have to go! Hurry!

283
00:54:18.888 --> 00:54:21.721
I've just received a signal
from the M-1 galaxy.

284
00:54:23.260 --> 00:54:26.388
Space monster Gigan has left.

285
00:55:43.206 --> 00:55:44.230
It's Jet Jaguar!

286
00:55:44.407 --> 00:55:46.170
Jet Jaguar is returning!

287
00:55:46.409 --> 00:55:47.205
Are you sure?

288
00:55:47.510 --> 00:55:48.670
Brother. look!

289
00:55:49.579 --> 00:55:50.603
Alright!

290
00:55:57.687 --> 00:55:59.552
Jet Jaguar!

291
00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:09.655
Professor. ask him if he
managed to bring Godzilla.

292
00:56:12.102 --> 00:56:12.966
Huh?

293
00:56:18.141 --> 00:56:19.369
That was strange...

294
00:56:19.909 --> 00:56:21.740
You didn't use the
ultra-sound transmitter.

295
00:56:24.080 --> 00:56:25.945
Jet Jaguar. come back here!

296
00:56:30.820 --> 00:56:33.311
Jet Jaguar. come back here!

297
00:56:38.395 --> 00:56:40.454
Well. this won't
work for us anymore.

298
00:56:41.464 --> 00:56:43.455
I set up Jet Jaguar's
programming with...

299
00:56:44.067 --> 00:56:46.331
...a feature that enables
it to act on its own.

300
00:56:46.503 --> 00:56:49.097
It's the survival program.
I'm sure of it.

301
00:56:49.305 --> 00:56:50.169
Survival?

302
00:56:52.275 --> 00:56:55.711
You mean that Jet Jaguar can't
be controlled by humans...

303
00:56:55.979 --> 00:56:58.140
...and it's thinking on its own?

304
00:58:41.784 --> 00:58:43.547
Hey. look over there.

305
00:58:43.720 --> 00:58:45.381
I know it looks
very dangerous...

306
00:58:45.622 --> 00:58:48.523
...but I'm the one
who built Jet Jaguar.

307
00:58:48.658 --> 00:58:49.989
I feel that I'm
responsible for him.

308
00:58:50.393 --> 00:58:53.794
I understand now. You're just like
a father concerned about his child.

309
00:59:56.125 --> 00:59:58.559
Jet Jaguar... he grew up.

310
01:00:26.923 --> 01:00:28.220
I don't believe it...

311
01:00:28.891 --> 01:00:29.858
But...

312
01:00:30.393 --> 01:00:32.987
...he must have seen that Godzilla
needed time in order to get here.

313
01:00:33.162 --> 01:00:36.928
Jet Jaguar must have programmed himself to
grow up in order to keep the monster here.

314
01:01:56.713 --> 01:01:58.840
That's Gigan. brother!

315
01:01:59.882 --> 01:02:01.315
Who's side is he on?

316
01:02:01.484 --> 01:02:02.416
That's not too hard to guess.

317
01:04:39.675 --> 01:04:41.540
Brother. it's Godzilla!

318
01:04:43.446 --> 01:04:44.913
Godzilla!

319
01:13:47.356 --> 01:13:49.950
Route all energy
to closing the portals.

320
01:13:50.125 --> 01:13:53.458
All units are to be on
immediate stand-by. Hurry!

321
01:16:56.378 --> 01:16:58.039
Seal all the portals
to the surface!

322
01:18:37.112 --> 01:18:37.806
Brother.

323
01:18:50.525 --> 01:18:53.688
You did it. Jet Jaguar!

324
01:18:54.162 --> 01:18:57.928
Jet Jaguar. thank you!

325
01:19:33.235 --> 01:19:36.170
Jet Jaguar. let's all go
home now. okay?

326
01:19:39.141 --> 01:19:42.076
Hey. let's all go home. okay?

327
01:19:42.477 --> 01:19:43.239
Hey!

328
01:19:44.212 --> 01:19:46.407
Hey. Jet Jaguar?

329
01:19:48.083 --> 01:19:49.516
Professor. the transmitter...

330
01:19:55.190 --> 01:19:57.590
Jet Jaguar. lets go home.

331
01:20:05.300 --> 01:20:07.200
What do you think happened?

332
01:20:16.211 --> 01:20:19.612
Of course. it's possible
he thinks his job is done.

333
01:20:20.982 --> 01:20:24.884
However. I'm not sure if he's just waiting
for the next time when he's needed again.

334
01:20:25.086 --> 01:20:26.986
Let's hope that day never comes.

335
01:20:27.155 --> 01:20:30.147
We should leave the people
beneath the sea in peace.

336
01:20:30.325 --> 01:20:32.190
They don't want to fight
any more than we do.

337
01:20:36.531 --> 01:20:40.297
Hey! Hey! Jet Jaguar!

338
01:20:42.137 --> 01:20:44.196
Jet Jaguar!

339
01:21:27.837 --> 01:21:31.396
THE END

340
01:21:31.637 --> 01:21:34.996
